{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.LayoutConflict","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.LayoutConflict","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Card","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.LayoutConflict.contiguous_layout_cannot_carry_a_colour_tube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.LayoutConflict.contiguous_layout_cannot_carry_a_colour_tube","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/LayoutConflict.lean#L103-L115","doc":"A colour tube needs `C` distinct couplings across one interface. For `C ≥ 2`\nthat is strictly more than the layout admits, so **no contiguous layout carries a\ncolour tube** — for any number of colours above one, hence in particular for\nthree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.LayoutConflict.at_most_one_coupling_per_interface","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.LayoutConflict.at_most_one_coupling_per_interface","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/LayoutConflict.lean#L95-L101","doc":"And there is at most one such coupling per interface — against the three a\ncolour tube needs. This is the general-`A` statement the exhaustive search\nverifies at `A = 2, 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.LayoutConflict.canonical_boundary_is_the_top_of_the_lower_block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.LayoutConflict.canonical_boundary_is_the_top_of_the_lower_block","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/LayoutConflict.lean#L84-L93","doc":"**The canonical layout's one boundary joins the TOP of nucleon `k` to the\nBOTTOM of nucleon `k+1`** — position `3k+2` to position `3k+3`. Reading positions\nwithin a nucleon as colours `0, 1, 2`, that is colour `2` to colour `0`: the one\navailable coupling is colour-MISMATCHED, before any question of how many there\nare. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.LayoutConflict.IsCoupling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.LayoutConflict.IsCoupling","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/LayoutConflict.lean#L79-L82","doc":"`x` is the lower endpoint of a single-generator coupling across the interface\n`(k, k+1)`: it lies in nucleon `k` and `x + 1` lies in nucleon `k+1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.LayoutConflict.nucleon_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.LayoutConflict.nucleon_gap","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/LayoutConflict.lean#L76-L77","doc":"Consecutive nucleon blocks are disjoint and correctly ordered. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.LayoutConflict.nucleonBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.LayoutConflict.nucleonBlock","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/LayoutConflict.lean#L73-L74","doc":"Nucleon `k`'s strands in the canonical layout. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.LayoutConflict.adjacent_pair_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.LayoutConflict.adjacent_pair_unique","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/LayoutConflict.lean#L50-L61","doc":"**The whole obstruction.** If a block ends strictly below where the next one\nstarts, the only way a member of the first is adjacent to a member of the second\nis at the single boundary pair: the top of the lower block and the bottom of the\nupper one.\n\nTwo disjoint intervals on a line touch once. Everything else in this file is a\nspecialisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.LayoutConflict.mem_block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.LayoutConflict.mem_block","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/LayoutConflict.lean#L47-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.LayoutConflict.block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.LayoutConflict.block","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/LayoutConflict.lean#L44-L45","doc":"The block of `C` consecutive positions starting at `p`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}